    fiber:{name:'Gray wool fiber',kind:'LAB · TRACE',desc:'A coarse gray wool fiber snagged on a nail at shoulder height. Consistent with a heavy coat; common in town, but not the scene custodians’ uniforms.'},
    token:{name:'Brass choir token',kind:'VERIFIED · SCENE',desc:'A tarnished token stamped with nine small notches. Parish ledgers call these “attendance counters”; the ninth notch is newer.'},
    witness:{name:'A voice at 9:13',kind:'WITNESS · UNCORROBORATED',desc:'Diner cook Jonah Pike remembers a calm voice asking whether the tower door still sticks. He recalls a smell of clove and wet wool.'},
    ledger:{name:'The Ninth Verse',kind:'DOCUMENT · VERIFIED',desc:'A marginal note in a 1938 hymn ledger: “When the bell speaks without a hand, the keeper must answer.” Initials S.C. appear in the same ink.'},
